WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>Kiss Day</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.780
<b>Old Aitheria - Palace Guard Barracks</b>

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:37.990
All done then.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:38.620
See you later.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:39.270
Sure.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:40.780
There he is!

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.370
Hans!

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.860
Nikolaus?

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.860
I know that face.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.490
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.490
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.850
You're going to that place, aren't you?

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:47.710
Yeah.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.370
Just got paid today.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.940
Then let's go together.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.000
After all, it's the day 
we've been waiting for.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.350
What day?

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.170
You really don't know?

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.820
It's kiss day!

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:00.890
What did you just say?

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.450
K-K-Kiss?

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:04.990
Kiss day?!

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.060
What? Kiss?

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.240
What do you mean by kiss day?

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.110
Yup, we're going to have fun tonight!

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.180
Nikolaus!

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.800
Damn you!

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.000
I told you you're staying here tonight!

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.990
<b>Berthold (32)
Company Commander of Aitheria Palace Guards
aka "the Devil"</b>

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.650
Weren't you listening?

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.960
Well, it's that...

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.130
I'm gonna fix that rotten 
attitude of yours right now.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.160
Get ready.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.060
But it's my kiss day!

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.670
Nikolaus, wait!

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.790
What in the world is this "kiss day"?

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.660
Help me!

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.340
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.020
Welcome!

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:38.940
Welcome.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.580
<i>They just opened, and they're 
already more full than normal.</i>

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.570
Hans-san, welcome.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.590
Is something wrong?

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.620
Uh, no, but Shinobu-chan,
I wanted to ask you something.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.330
Yes, what is it?

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.750
Oh, nothing.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.670
I'll have a whatsontap.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.380
Certainly.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.770
<i>She sure looks cheerful.</i>

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.900
Let's see what the appetizer is.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.920
<b>Chicken and Taro Stew</b>

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.920
<b>A happy dish with varied textures</b>

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.920
Looks like chicken and taro potatoes!

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.630
<i>So tender!</i>

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.990
<i>The meat fibers are soft 
enough to fall apart,</i>

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.020
<b>Fall Fall</b>

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.580
<i>allowing the robust flavors to 
spread their wings in your mouth!</i>

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.060
<b>Fall</b>

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.060
And next, we have...

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:33.060
<b>Slip</b>

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.960
<i>Got to get a careful grip on this 
taro so it doesn't slip away.</i>

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.180
<i>This rich texture is a real treat!</i>

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:45.880
<b>Rich~</b>

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.360
<i>Quite a different texture from kartoffel.</i>

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.020
Hans-san, you've really gotten 
good with the chopsticks.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:54.100
You noticed? I've been 
practicing on the down low.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.330
Don't want to have the 
other guys pull ahead.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.320
Nikolaus-san and Berthold-san 
are also very good.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.820
Everyone from the palace guard learns fast.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.270
Here's your draft beer. Thanks for waiting.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.730
Thank you!

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.990
<i>This is it!</i>

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.300
<b>Fizz</b>

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.970
<i>I just can't get enough of this smooth,</i>

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.340
<b>Fizz</b>

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.110
<i>bitter taste that goes 
right down your throat!</i>

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.110
<b>Fizz</b>

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.930
So, what should I order today?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:27.610
<i>This is a good time to look around and 
see what everyone else is eating.</i>

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:31.110
<i>Hmm, that looks like an appetizer, too.</i>

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.500
Hey, Taishou.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.130
Does every customer get 
a different appetizer?

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.850
You've noticed.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:41.260
I tailor the amount and type of appetizer 
to the individual tastes of the customer.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.670
I'm not surprised; you are very attentive.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.380
Hans-san, what can I bring 
for you to eat and drink?

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.810
I think I'll have some reishu.
Also what's today's special?

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.160
Today's special, huh?

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.510
Yeah, what is it?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.530
What's going on Shinobu-chan? 
Did something good happen?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.690
Well actually, today is kiss day.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.830
K-K-K-K-Kiss?

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.190
Kiss day?

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.650
That's right, today is kiss day.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.650
The truth is, I have a weakness for it.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.960
<i>She says she has a weakness?!</i>

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.980
<i>So </i>that's<i> why there's so 
many people here tonight!</i>

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.010
<i>They're all here for kiss day!</i>

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.230
We have a lot of kiss today.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.170
A lot?!

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.910
I'm so excited!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.310
She's excited!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.600
<i>So what is this kiss day 
supposed to be, anyway?</i>

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.730
<i>Some kind of festival?</i>

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:44.100
<i>Kisses are exchanged with 
partners, one after another.</i>

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.590
<i>That kind of festival?!</i>

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.540
<i>No, no, no, no!</i>

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:55.850
<i>I can't imagine our sweet Shinobu 
engaged in anything so lewd!</i>

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.110
<i>Then again, this store is serving 
never-before-seen foods of another land.</i>

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:05.020
<i>It's possible that this is a regular 
custom back in Taishou's land.</i>

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.280
<i>That reminds me. We've got a 
new deacon over at the church.</i>

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.700
<i>He seemed like a straight-laced old man.</i>

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.680
<i>If he ever got wind of this custom...</i>

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.310
We will drive out this heretical evil!

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.820
<i>I don't think Nobu would survive that!</i>

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.930
<i>This is bad! Real bad!</i>

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.840
<i>If I don't have my meals 
at Nobu to look forward to,</i>

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.310
<i>what the hell am I even going to live for?</i>

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.700
I like it, too. Kiss.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.030
<i>I like it, too. Kiss.</i>

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.430
<i>I like it, too. Kiss. Kiss...</i>

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.720
<i>Kissing Taishou?!</i>

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.960
You know, I don't really 
think that's for me.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.060
I think this is some kind of 
strange misunderstanding.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.390
"Kisu" is the name of a fish.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:55.460
What?

00:05:55.470 --> 00:06:01.470
<b>Fish
Joy</b>

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:59.370
Back in our country, we write it's name 
using the characters "joyful" and "fish."

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.190
It's considered an auspicious fish.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:04.330
I-I see.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.490
<i>It was a fish.</i>

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.810
<i>I'm glad.</i>

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:11.900
<i>But... also a little disappointed.</i>

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.410
Is something wrong?

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.050
Nothing at all.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:19.750
So a joyful fish, huh? It has a good ring.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.150
Right?

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.850
And if you fry it up in 
tempura, it's <i>so</i> good.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.450
I'll have an order of that kisu tempura.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.280
Me, too!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:30.990
Me, too!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:31.770
Me, too!

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:32.880
Coming right up!

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.870
Today's kisu is excellent!

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.480
<b>Sizzle~</b>

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.890
<b>Sizzle Sizzle Sizzle</b>

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.530
Hans-san, pardon my reach.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.590
What's this?

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:05.050
It's paper. Tempura is best 
enjoyed eaten off of this paper.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:08.550
What does she mean, "best enjoyed"?

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.030
Here you are.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.540
Kisu tempura.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:14.550
<b>Kisu Tempura</b>

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:14.550
<b>Shinobu-chan's favorite! 
You must try this tempura</b>

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:18.150
You should eat the tempura dipped 
in salt or the dipping sauce.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.430
Then I'll start off with the salt.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:28.530
<b>Crunch</b>

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:30.630
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.030
Wow!

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.900
It's materialized fluffiness!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.040
<b>Crunch</b>

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.650
<i>It's so much lighter than I imagined!</i>

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:44.110
<i>Unlike schnitzel or fried chicken, 
this has an amazing lightness to it.</i>

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.810
<i>How is this texture possible 
when it's fried in fat?</i>

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.550
Wait, it's the paper!

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.750
<i>The paper absorbs the excess fat.</i>

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.060
<i>That's why it's so light, 
even though it's fried.</i>

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.560
<i>That's how this perfect harmony is born!</i>

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.440
Is this green thing paprika?

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.600
<b>Cool</b>

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.650
<i>What a refreshing flavor!</i>

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.100
<b>Cool</b>

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:11.120
<i>This is bursting with a refreshing aroma!</i>

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:13.860
<i>It's a wonderful contrast 
and resets your palate!</i>

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.310
<b>Cool</b>

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.570
<i>And now we use this ten tsuyu.</i>

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:18.430
<b>Crunch</b>

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.450
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.930
<i>This sauce called "ten tsuyu!"</i>

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.770
<i>Despite being transparent, it's got 
a surprising amount of body,</i>

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.340
<i>and it pairs excellently with 
the light meat of the kisu.</i>

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:30.330
<i>I could eat this forever.</i>

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.850
<i>And then this reishu.</i>

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:35.090
<b>Crisp</b>

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:38.340
<i>This crisp, bold taste goes so 
well with the light, fried kisu.</i>

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.800
<b>Crisp</b>

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:40.220
Taishou, I'll have another order!

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:40.890
Coming up.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:41.720
Me, too.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:42.830
Me, too.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.470
I'll take a double order!

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:49.240
Did you know that kisu tempura 
goes really well on a tendon, too?

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.490
Tendon?

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:51.890
I've never heard of that before.

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.050
I'll have one of those!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:53.830
Me, too!

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.670
Me, too!

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:55.620
A big one!

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:56.620
Me, too!

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:57.390
Me, too!

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.090
Me, too!

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.230
Me, too!

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:03.940
Hey, if everyone eats that much of 
it, there won't be any left for me!

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.510
I'm sorry, Shinobu-chan, but 
I'm not holding back today.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:09.810
I just got paid!

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:12.640
I'm not leaving until I'm full.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.600
But...

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.350
And then, you really fooled me back there.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:18.860
Now we're even.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.090
Fooled you?

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:21.620
What are you talking about?

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.640
So go ahead, Taishou.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:24.200
Coming right up.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.130
Hey, but what am I going to eat then?

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.380
What about my kisu day?

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.480
Hey, smells great!

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.580
Welcome.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.500
Nikolaus.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:37.810
Shinobu-chan, I'll have a whatsontap 
and some kisu tempura.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:41.240
Nikolaus, you knew all along?

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:44.880
Of course I did. I told 
you today is kisu day.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:46.510
Right, Shinobu-chan?

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.230
That's not what I meant!

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.500
Wait, did you hear about this from him, too?

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.470
You, too? I heard today was kiss day.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:56.010
That means...

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:59.090
Wait, what? Did I do something wrong?

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:01.550
Shinobu-chan, I'm sorry I accused you.

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:04.020
He's the one in the wrong.

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.760
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:07.860
One kisu tendon.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.260
<b>Kisu Tendon</b>

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.260
<b>An irresistible dish when you 
put the special sauce on it!</b>

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.250
We'll be putting them out one 
after another, Shinobu-chan.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:18.370
Shinobu-chan had been looking 
forward to this kisu day.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:23.510
Unfortunately, it looks like there 
won't be much left for her.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:27.570
My kisu!

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:39.980
<b>Roppongi: Imoaraizaka</b>

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:38.350
Roppongi is famous for being 
the pleasure district,

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:41.250
and all sorts of people congregate here.

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:42.150
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:45.020
When you come all the way down from 
Roppongi, you arrive here at Imoaraizaka.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:50.430
I am here because I'm 
looking for that thing.

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:51.810
That thing! Let's go!

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:55.690
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.450
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:58.150
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu".

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.180
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.440
You know what I mean by that thing, right?

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.070
Of course!

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:05.120
<b>Kisu tempura, of course</b>

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.500
Kisu tempura, of course.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:06.180
I'm actually... I can't take it anymore.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.110
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi.</b>

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.900
I just want to have that and chug!

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:09.510
I couldn't agree more!

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.710
Could this be the place I'm looking for?

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:13.650
It already looks the part 
of being a great place, no?

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.780
Welcome, come in!

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:14.990
Hello.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:15.780
Come in.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:18.040
Tempura Mikaku is a famous for 
their homegrown vegetables and

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:19.420
<b>Tempura Mikaku</b>

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.410
their "Edomae" fish.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.290
What do you recommend?

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:21.590
<b>Tempura Mikaku
 2nd Generation Owner:  Mori Kouji-san</b>

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:20.920
All right.

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:21.600
Right here.

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:23.790
And that brown stuff, with foam and stuff?

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.120
Okay, I got you.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:26.640
One draft beer!

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:29.340
First, a whatsontap.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.700
Oh my, it always looks so good.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:39.870
You know, when everybody is still 
working, to be drinking one of these?

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.100
Yes, what's it like?

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:45.720
I feel like I'll get smote, or cursed. 
But it's never happened to me. Never.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.370
Ah-ah. And the first recommended item is?

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.200
Daikon radish.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:52.230
How rare, daikon.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.960
How is the taste of the 
homegrown vegetables?

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:56.930
This is daikon.

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:58.800
I know, I'm asking about the taste!

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:57.840
Isn't it?

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.920
How did you come up with this?

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:00.990
Here, broccoli.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.080
Broccoli.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:03.530
Pretty rare to see
that in tempura form.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.420
Are all the items
going to be heretical?

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:06.980
What kind of things do
 you want to eat?

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.260
What's making me a bit scared 
is that I see banana there.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:09.860
I do have banana.

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:10.820
Pickled radish?

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:11.800
It was not good.

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:13.680
It was not? But you tried it?

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.990
Wow, the boss is brave!

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:19.660
Now that you've enjoyed the 
vegetables, let's ask for the kisu.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.770
For everything, the base 
is the Edomae style.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:25.260
The vegetables are fro
 your own field.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.100
That's right.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.390
Those are also Edomae.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.750
Yes, they are.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.200
Because people from
Edo are making them.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:34.260
I think it's almost done.

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:35.120
Here you go, kisu.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:36.340
It's good.

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:38.090
There it is! Today's mission!

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:40.660
I watched the show earlier, and 
that's the same for you too, right?

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.630
I bet you want to eat 
kisu tempura now, right?

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.180
You are so right!

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.900
I'm going to have the
 kisu with ten tsuyu.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.560
This fine white fish
 is too good!

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:51.870
It's hot.

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:52.510
It's hot.

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:53.050
Hot.

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:55.660
That's why you dip it in the sauce. 
So you can eat it right away.

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:57.590
I see. When you put it in your mouth, 
it just melts and releases its flavors.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:02.790
The kisu's light tastiness is doubled 
when you make it into tempura.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.190
I only get one?

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:07.070
You can have as
 many as you want.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:09.100
Until you tap out.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.250
Whoa, let's not go that far.

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:12.300
I can easily do 5-6 pieces!

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:15.700
Yeah, tempura really does have 
the Edomae feeling to it.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:21.370
Next, please do some
Japanese prawns.

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:24.310
Hey, Nagira-san, did you beg 
Nobu to do something?!

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:27.000
Even Nagira-san approves of 
this place, Tempura Mikaku.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:29.060
<b>Assistance: Gurunabi                                 To be continued</b>

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.580
It's a five minute walk from Roppongi.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.090
If you want to have good kisu 
tempura, come here. Come here!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:58.010
<b>Next Time...
The Burglar</b>

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:54.360
Next time on "Isekai Izakaya"
aka "Izakaya Nobu in Aitheria."

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:57.470
Please sample the tasty tales.
